From 2aff5d1df770dfa891d4d80592ae564fa761acd9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Wason <wason@wasontech.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:58:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] Use lowercase Windows SDK header names

MinGW-w64 installs the Windows SDK headers in lowercase (winsock2.h,
windows.h, shlobj.h, ...). On a case-sensitive file system, which is what a
Linux cross-build uses, the mixed-case includes are not found. MSVC is
case-insensitive, so lowercase names work for both toolchains.

All changes are inside ROBOTRACONTEUR_WINDOWS blocks or Windows-only sources.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
